<script>
  // Only the kb's own data and logic, as exported: no new files in src/lib.
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { causeOf, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  const REPO = 'https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows/issues';
  const TICKETS = [
    { issue: 1, problem: 'parser', title: 'Shared date parser reads day-first dates month first' },
    { issue: 2, problem: 'hint', title: 'booking-v3 form tells day-first tenants to type MM/DD/YYYY' },
    { issue: 3, problem: 'one-day', title: 'Invites land one day off across time zones' },
  ];

  // One id, one report. A report the desk read as a one-day move is that problem; the rest go by tenant.
  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const problemOf = (r) => (notes.oneDayMove.includes(r.id) ? 'one-day' : causeOf(r, tenantOf(r)) ?? 'unplaced');
  const rows = TICKETS.map((t) => {
    const rs = merged.filter((r) => problemOf(r) === t.problem);
    const days = rs.map((r) => r.receivedAt.slice(0, 10)).sort();
    return { ...t, reports: rs.length, tenants: new Set(rs.map((r) => r.tenant)).size, first: days[0], last: days[days.length - 1] };
  });
  const placed = rows.reduce((n, r) => n + r.reports, 0);
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says the date reports are one issue with one fix queued. The reports
say otherwise. They were merged on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and "wrong date" is a subject that more than one bug produces.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is the parser fix. It closes <a href="{REPO}/1">#1</a> only.
<a href="{REPO}/2">#2</a> and <a href="{REPO}/3">#3</a> stay open after it ships.
</Callout>

## The problems in #4471

<p><strong>{merged.length}</strong> reports merged into #4471 · <strong>{rows.length}</strong> problems ·
<strong>{placed}</strong> placed in a ticket of their own</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>ticket</th><th>problem</th><th>reports</th><th>tenants</th><th>seen</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {#each rows as r (r.issue)}
      <tr>
        <td><a href="{REPO}/{r.issue}">#{r.issue}</a> {r.title}</td>
        <td><code>{r.problem}</code></td>
        <td>{r.reports}</td>
        <td>{r.tenants}</td>
        <td>{r.first} → {r.last}</td>
      </tr>
    {/each}
  </tbody>
</table>

The table is computed from the ticket export when the page renders, with the desk's own logic
(`causes.ts`, `locales.ts`, `desk-notes.json`), so the counts follow the queue.

## How a report is placed

1. Count each report once: the export pages overlap, so the same id can appear twice.
2. If the desk read it as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), it goes to #3.
3. Otherwise ask the tenant, not the reporter's browser (`causes.ts`): a day-first tenant on a
   `booking-v3` form goes to #2; every other day-first report goes to #1.

Intake's tag is not used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser and often names the wrong
cause: compare the "tagged as" column on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471).

## What each problem is

**#1 `parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and
month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July.

**#2 `hint`** — `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as
told, and the form reads the value the tenant's way. Same symptom as #1, different code, different fix.

**#3 `one-day`** — the date moves by one day, not by a swap: Tuesday becomes Monday, a client in
Lisbon and a client in Toronto see different days for the same meeting, an invite arrives before the
booking. That is time-zone handling, not parsing. By tenant these reports file under `parser`; the
#4471 page only footnotes them.

## For the desk

- Merge into a ticket only reports with the same problem, not the same subject.
- When a new date report comes in, place it with the steps above and add it to that ticket.
- Do not close the date reports when the parser fix ships; #2 and #3 need their own fixes.

